const repo="RGCsAGupta/driftlens";
const body=`## Summary

- add manual, terminal, persisted explanation state without changing deterministic scan truth
- send only the bounded allowlisted comparison projection through the official OpenAI Responses Structured Outputs helper
- enforce \`store: false\`, 12-second timeout, 900-token output bound, and SDK \`maxRetries: 0\`
- require explicit server-side key and model configuration; document \`gpt-5.6\` as the initial model value
- add explanation API, operator UI states, rollback-compatible additive persistence, restart reuse, OpenAPI contract, documentation, and evidence inventory
- preserve SQLite \`user_version = 1\` so the previous immutable image can ignore explanation columns and pass readiness after rollback
- exclude live-only injected sidecars from provider input

## Verification

- focused local correction gates: Prettier, ESLint with zero warnings, strict TypeScript, repository tests 7/7, and \`git diff --check\`
- rollback regression reproduces the last-known-good version guard, readiness write/rollback, and legacy-column read against the migrated database
- trusted exact-head run [30644360641](https://github.com/RGCsAGupta/driftlens/actions/runs/30644360641) passed verify job [91201941111](https://github.com/RGCsAGupta/driftlens/actions/runs/30644360641/job/91201941111)
- trusted gates: format, lint, typecheck, 132 tests, 89.63% overall line coverage, scanner regression, production build, Playwright E2E, dependency audit, and secret scan
- private release correctly skipped on the feature branch; no provider or network call made

Closes #11`;
const update=await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_update_pull_request({repository_full_name:repo,pr_number:21,body});
text(JSON.stringify(update));
const comment=`## P1 rollback correction — exact head \`05d0e977c5afbe4b9a81100653ccfdc21841a82e\`

Finding confirmed. The earlier \`user_version = 2\` migration prevented the last-known-good image from opening the database.

Correction:

- explanation columns are discovered with \`PRAGMA table_info(scans)\` and added idempotently while retaining \`user_version = 1\`;
- databases touched by the unmerged version-2 implementation are repaired back to version 1 without deleting explanation data;
- the rollback regression runs the previous binary's version guard, readiness insert/rollback, and legacy-column read against the migrated database;
- README now states the tested rollback contract.

Evidence:

- focused local: Prettier, ESLint, strict TypeScript, repository tests 7/7, \`git diff --check\`;
- trusted exact-head run [30644360641](https://github.com/RGCsAGupta/driftlens/actions/runs/30644360641) passed verify job [91201941111](https://github.com/RGCsAGupta/driftlens/actions/runs/30644360641/job/91201941111): 132 tests, 89.63% overall line coverage, 86% repository line coverage, build, Playwright E2E, audit, and secret scans;
- private-release [91202538409](https://github.com/RGCsAGupta/driftlens/actions/runs/30644360641/job/91202538409) correctly skipped on the feature branch.

Final re-review found no remaining correctness, security, test, documentation, rollback, dependency, or evidence blocker. Merge still requires explicit user approval of exact head \`05d0e977c5afbe4b9a81100653ccfdc21841a82e\`.`;
const c=await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_add_comment_to_issue({repo_full_name:repo,pr_number:21,comment});
text(JSON.stringify(c));
const ready=await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_mark_pull_request_ready_for_review({repository_full_name:repo,pr_number:21});
text(JSON.stringify(ready));

